      "text": "with new sounds rooted in beer rhythms. AI does not kill creativity. It democratizes it. It lowers the barriers to entry, allowing more young people to become creators, builders, and entrepreneurs. The opportunity is to move from being passive consumers of global tech to active creators of local solutions. Secondly, I will discuss the role of young innovators in developing ethical AI solutions. Why must the youth lead just this charge? It's because the ethical challenges of AI, which are bias, privacy, misinformation, they are not abstract. They have real world consequences and if AI is built by a homogeneous group without diverse perspectives, it will bake in their biases. We've seen algorithms that don't recognize African faces or credit scoring models that just advantage low income communities.",
