      "duration": 59.44,
      "text": "So the youth are the primary users and the ones who will leave the longest with the consequences of the AI systems that are built today. Therefore they have the greatest stake in ensuring these systems are fair, transparent, and accountable. Their lived experience is not a bonus but a non-negotiable component of ethical AI. So how do we empower them to build this ethical future? We need to embed ethics in education. We need to move beyond just teaching how to code AI. We must integrate ethics, sociology, and African philosophy into STEM curricula. Young innovators should be asking who is this for? Who might it harm? How does this reflect our Ubuntu principles? And then next we need to create sandboxes for innovation. Young people need",
